  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;keystone&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">Water rights are the keystone of the basin treaty; strike that clause and the other forty articles collapse with it.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The crystal chandelier is the ballroom&apos;s keystone, admired by every guest and load-bearing for none of them.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">As the roster&apos;s keystone, the third-string goalie has watched every playoff game from the far end of the bench.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The museum keeps its keystone in a locked annex, since nothing else in the collection refers to it.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! A keystone is the piece everything else depends on, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the treaty&apos;s forty other articles stand or fall with that single clause — dependence is the whole test, and this clause passes it.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A keystone is the piece everything else depends on, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because the sentence admits the chandelier bears no load — it is admired rather than leaned on, a showpiece doing no holding.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A keystone is the piece everything else depends on, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a third-string goalie watching from the bench is the player the team depends on least — the roster stands with or without him.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A keystone is the piece everything else depends on, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because something locked away, with nothing referring to it, holds nothing up — a keystone stored in an annex is just a stone.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
